  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-08,NFR-06">BFF query-filter enforcement: message-level + thread-level privacy, internal-only (D-05 user attribute), privilege classification (composes with privacy; AI may flag never decide — ADR-015). Point-forward switch — prior private messages stay restricted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06-SECURITY">Security-sensitive (root §6): no privileged/private content leaks; ACS membership never exceeds Dataverse-derived access (agree with task 041). Explicit `code-review` + `adr-check` at Step 9.5 are REQUIRED. Default-deny on ambiguity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design-§5">Compose from EXISTING Dataverse record security — do NOT rebuild core access control. The Dataverse record is the authoritative access boundary; the SPE archive holds no separate ACL we depend on.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">AI may FLAG but NEVER DECIDE privilege. Enforcement acts on the classification field only; MUST NOT call AI or act on an AI verdict at read time.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Thread anchor for record-scoped checks reuses the regarding family — MUST NOT add a second regarding mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Point-forward privacy switch: opening a private thread exposes only messages from that moment forward; retroactive open is a separate audited action, OUT of R1 — do NOT build bulk-open tooling.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003,ADR-008">Enforce via existing BFF authorization seams + endpoint filters; ProblemDetails on denial (ADR-019).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-§10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

