    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Compose from record security (default-deny)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/">
        Start from Dataverse record readability, then subtract: message/thread privacy (no grant → hide), internal-only (non-internal → hide), point-forward (message timestamp before open → stay restricted). Deny wins; a row is visible only if it passes every dimension.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Flag-never-decide (ADR-015)" location=".claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-flag-never-decide.md">
        Privilege enforcement reads the classification field a human owns; AI may suggest the flag upstream. No AI call at read time.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Point-forward switch" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/">
        On open, compare each message's timestamp to the thread's privacy-open timestamp; messages before it remain restricted. No retroactive exposure.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read task 005's privacy/internal-only/privilege columns on `sprk_communication`/`sprk_communicationthread`, task 040's `IThreadResolver` (thread identity), task 002's private-grant decision, and the existing BFF authorization seams/endpoint filters (ADR-003/008). Confirm how task 041 derives the authorized set (must agree).</step>
    <step order="2">Read design §5, `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F, root §11, ADR-015, ADR-034 before designing the filter. Note the security-sensitive escalation posture (root §6 / §6.5).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the composition filter (default-deny) applied on the BFF read path for `sprk_communication` / thread reads: (a) base Dataverse record readability; (b) message-level privacy — hidden without grant; (c) thread-level privacy — thread hidden without an explicit per-record grant (task 002 primitive); (d) internal-only — hidden from non-internal users via the D-05 attribute; (e) privilege classification — composes with privacy, acts on the field only (ADR-015). A row is visible only if it passes EVERY dimension.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the point-forward privacy switch: record a privacy-open timestamp when a thread is opened; the filter keeps messages authored before that timestamp restricted. No retroactive exposure; no bulk-open tooling (out of R1).</step>
    <step order="5">Ensure the read filter agrees with task 041's membership projection — both derive from Dataverse-derived access; neither may exceed it. Add an assertion/test that the filtered read set never includes a message the ACS-membership projection would exclude.</step>
    <step order="6">Return ProblemDetails (ADR-019) on explicit denial paths; register the filter/service via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional.</step>
    <step order="7">Write security enforcement tests (closed set, incl. negative/authorization cases): a private thread's messages are INVISIBLE to a user without a grant; an internal-only message is INVISIBLE to a non-internal user; a privileged message is not returned to an unauthorized caller; flipping a thread to open exposes ONLY messages after the open timestamp (prior private messages stay restricted); the read filter set ⊆ Dataverse-derived access (agrees with 041); AI is NOT called at read time (ADR-015).</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` then `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-042-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates — UNCONDITIONALLY REQUIRED (security-sensitive, NFR-06): `code-review` on the diff with explicit focus on leak paths, default-deny, point-forward correctness, ADR-015 flag-never-decide, and agreement with task 041's projection; `adr-check` against `spec.md`. Address ALL Critical findings before PR. Per root §6, treat any ambiguity as a human-escalation trigger; per §6.5, surface any ADR tension rather than silently complying.</step>
    <step order="9.6">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path).</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (042 ✅) + reset `current-task.md`; record decisions (filter composition order, point-forward timestamp source, grant primitive used, 041-agreement assertion).</step>
  </steps>

